    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r3:t2",
    "narration": "The floor is quiet. Two beds stand against the wall, each with its stool and nightstand, the wardrobes beside them still bare. Opposite, the wooden medical-storage cabinets wait empty. Light from the tall windows falls across the stone floor in wide, pale slabs.\n\nIris sits on the near bed's edge, her hands resting in her lap. She glances toward the windows, then back. Her shoulders ease a fraction. \"This is fine,\" she says, and after a beat adds, \"Quieter than I expected up here.\" Her voice stays low, matched to the stillness of the room and the house rule about shared reading hours.\n\nThe spiral stair opens at the perimeter behind her, its steps descending toward the ground floor and rising toward the next level. Neither direction carries sound. The air is cool and dry, carrying only the faint mineral smell of old stone.",
